From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): use systemd-ukify, not the dropped ukify package

Fedora no longer ships a standalone `ukify` package -- /usr/bin/ukify
moved into systemd-ukify -- so building the mkosi tools tree against a
current Fedora fails with:

    No match for argument: ukify
    Error: Unable to find a match: ukify

This is invisible on a developer machine whose tools tree was cached
while the old package still existed. It bites any cold cache: a fresh
clone, a new workstation, or CI.

mkosi's own default tools packages already include systemd-ukify, so
naming it here is belt-and-braces rather than strictly required; keeping
the explicit entry preserves upstream's intent that the tools tree is
guaranteed to carry ukify.
---
 mkosi.conf | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mkosi.conf b/mkosi.conf
index 6d81ebc..9bc8f01 100644
--- a/mkosi.conf
+++ b/mkosi.conf
@@ -19,7 +19,13 @@ CacheDirectory=mkosi.cache
 Incremental=no
 ToolsTreePackages=
 	erofs-utils
-	ukify
+	# systemd-ukify, not ukify. Fedora dropped the standalone `ukify`
+	# package -- /usr/bin/ukify now ships in systemd-ukify -- so a
+	# tools tree built against current Fedora fails with
+	# "No match for argument: ukify". Existing checkouts only survive
+	# it because their tools tree was cached while the old package
+	# still existed; any cold cache hits it.
+	systemd-ukify
 	# binutils for objcopy: mkosi.finalize extracts UKI .linux + .initrd
 	# sections to /boot/kernel_2712.img + /boot/initramfs_2712 for Pi
 	# firmware boot (no UEFI on Pi 5, so the UKI itself isn't loaded —
-- 
